{"task_id": "HumanEval/52", "solution": "def _validate_inputs(l: list, t: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Validates the types of input l and t, and elements of l.\n    Raises TypeError if any validation fails.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(l, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'l' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(t, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 't' must be an integer.\")\n    for item in l:\n        if not isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(f\"All elements in list 'l' must be numbers, but found type {type(item).__name__}.\")\n\ndef below_threshold(l: list, t: int):\n    \"\"\"Return True if all numbers in the list l are below threshold t.\n    >>> below_threshold([1, 2, 4, 10], 100)\n    True\n    >>> below_threshold([1, 20, 4, 10], 5)\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_inputs(l, t)\n\n    if not l:\n        return True\n\n    for number in l:\n        if number >= t:\n            return False\n    return True"}
